# Advisories that are present in a Solver image but not reachable from it.
#
# Every entry must state which image carries it, why the vulnerable code cannot
# be reached, why it is not simply fixed by an upgrade, and what would let the
# entry be removed. An entry without that is a suppression, not a decision.
#
# Anything not listed here still fails the release scan.

# GHSA-r277-6w6q-xmqw / kin-openapi ValidationHandler.Load() fail-open
#
# Carried by: nuclei, in tga-kali-ctf-web, tga-kali-surface-mapper,
#             tga-kali-vulnerability-validator, tga-kali-web-api-analyst
# Present at: github.com/getkin/kin-openapi v0.132.0
#
# Not reachable: the advisory is in kin-openapi's server-side request
# validation middleware. nuclei imports only openapi2, openapi2conv and
# openapi3 -- the specification parsers -- and contains no reference to
# kin-openapi/routers or ValidationHandler. It reads OpenAPI documents to
# generate requests; it never serves or validates them.
#
# Not fixed by upgrading: no released nuclei uses a fixed kin-openapi. v3.8.0
# through v3.11.0 all pin v0.132.0, and forcing v0.144.0 fails to compile --
# pkg/input/formats/openapi/examples.go:179 and :191 break on its changed API.
# Clearing this properly would mean carrying a patched nuclei fork.
#
# Remove when: nuclei upstream moves to kin-openapi >= 0.144.0. Re-check on any
# nuclei bump.
GHSA-r277-6w6q-xmqw

# CVE-2025-68121 / Go stdlib crypto/tls incorrect certificate validation
#
# Carried by: frida, in tga-kali-dynamic-analysis
# Present at: frida/_frida.abi3.so, a prebuilt wheel built with go1.24.3
#             (fixed in Go 1.24.13 / 1.25.7)
#
# Not reachable: the flaw is in TLS certificate validation, and the
# dynamic-analysis-v1 profile runs with network_mode "none" and allow_net_raw
# false. A container with no network cannot complete a TLS handshake, so the
# validation path is never entered. frida is used here to instrument local
# processes, not to reach anything remote.
#
# Not fixed by upgrading: the Go version is baked into frida's published
# wheel, not chosen by this repository. frida 17.16.4 and 17.17.0 -- the
# pinned and the newest release -- both report go1.24.3 under `go version`.
# Clearing it would mean building frida-core from source.
#
# Remove when: a frida release ships a wheel built with Go >= 1.24.13. Check
# with `go version <site-packages>/frida/_frida.abi3.so` on any frida bump.
CVE-2025-68121
